      "id": "nl929e0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Parliament of India consists of three components: the President, the Lok Sabha (House of the People), and the Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Lok Sabha represents the people of India directly, whereas Rajya Sabha represents the states and Union Territories.",
        "Parliament conducts three standard sessions annually: Budget Session, Monsoon Session, and Winter Session.",
        "Legislative proposals pass through distinct stages for Ordinary, Money, Financial, and Constitutional Amendment Bills.",
        "Executive accountability is enforced by Parliament through questions, motions, and financial control."
      ],
      "id": "43gw5kz"
    },
