      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Money Bills (Article 110) can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha with prior recommendation of the President.",
        "A Joint Sitting (Article 108) is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha, not the Chairman of Rajya Sabha.",
        "Rajya Sabha possesses exclusive constitutional powers under Article 249 (legislating on State List) and Article 312 (creating All-India Services)."
      ],
      "id": "se2ecqs"
